cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EASA: Embedded Action Selection Architecture -- a basal ganglia robot model under realistic contact physics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Montes González"
    given-names: "Fernando"
    affiliation: "Universidad Veracruzana"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/TODO"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ferdiex/easa"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"          # TODO: bump alongside git tags, e.g. v0.1-easa
date-released: "TODO-YYYY-MM-DD"
keywords:
  - basal ganglia
  - action selection
  - neurorobotics
  - computational neuroscience
  - Khepera
  - PyBullet
abstract: >
  A Python/PyBullet port of the basal ganglia model by Prescott et al.
  (2006), implementing the embedded action selection architecture (EASA)
  with the real geometry of the Khepera I robot and its gripper, running
  the original foraging task under a modern rigid-body physics engine.

